   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to repeal subdivision 6 of section 51 of the public authorities law,\nrelating to voting by members of the New York state authorities control board",
    "basePrintNo": "S7337",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7337-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 28,
       "fullName": "Liz Krueger",
       "imgName": "401_liz_krueger.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 401,
       "sessionMemberId": 1820,
       "sessionYear": 2021,
       "shortName": "KRUEGER"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Rpld §51 sub 6, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7337    Revised 5/18/22\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to repeal subdivision 6 of section 51 of the public authorities\nlaw, relating to voting by members of the New York state authorities\ncontrol board\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nRemoves changes to the PACB statute enacted by demand of the Governor in\n2019.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill repeals subdivision 6 of section 51 of the public authorities\nlaw, relating to voting by members of the New York state authorities\ncontrol board.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis particular provision was laid upon the table in the waning days of\nthe FY 2019-20 New York State Budget Process. It received no sunlight,\ndebate or review. Since it created a disproportionate power dynamic\nadvantaging only the Executive, repeal is not only wise but well\nwarranted.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill in 2021.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone anticipated to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediate.\n",
